IT Security Analyst (Remote)
Location: Richmond, VA
Duration: 12 Months

Work Arrangement: Remote
Interview: In-person only (no exceptions)
Note: Candidates must reside in Virginia or within a reasonable distance of Richmond, VA. Occasional onsite meetings may be required.
Job Description
We are seeking an experienced IT Security Analyst to support cybersecurity governance, risk management, compliance, privacy, and security assessments.
Key Responsibilities
•	Conduct security risk assessments, Business Impact Analyses (BIAs), data classification, and control assessments.
•	Maintain risk registers, remediation plans, and compliance records using Archer GRC or similar platforms.
•	Apply security frameworks, including NIST SP 800-53, VITA SEC530, and CIS Controls, along with applicable regulatory requirements.
•	Support IT audits, evidence collection, compliance reviews, and corrective-action tracking.
•	Review vendor security assessments, SOC reports, and data-sharing agreements.
•	Develop security policies, procedures, assessment reports, and executive summaries.
•	Support security awareness, incident response governance, business continuity, and AI risk assessments.
Required Qualifications
•	5+ years of experience in cybersecurity, information security, or IT risk management.
•	4+ years of experience with NIST security frameworks, including NIST SP 800-53.
•	3+ years of experience in GRC, security assessments, IT audits, and remediation tracking.
•	Strong documentation, analytical, communication, and stakeholder management skills.
Preferred Qualifications
•	Experience with Archer GRC, VITA SEC530, and third-party risk management.
•	Knowledge of CJIS, VCIN, HIPAA, PCI DSS, FERPA, and FTI compliance requirements.
•	Certifications such as CRISC, CISA, CGRC, CISSP, or CISM.

